      "writtenOn": "2024-11-11T21:20:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like you\u0027re mixing up the `fp_maintenance(void)` function and the [`int elan_fp_maintenance(uint16_t *error_state)`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/driver/fingerprint/elan/elan_sensor_pal.c;l\u003d206;drc\u003d0e2ec3e7e7920f033e414885df85f1cbcc091f41) functions.\n\nThe `fp_maintenance(void)` function does not take any arguments. When building for elan, it calls the `int elan_fp_maintenance(uint16_t *error_state)`, which always passes a pointer to `static uint16_t errors;` (will never be `NULL`).",
      "parentUuid": "d5960a66_5f0f9fe9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 169,
        "startChar": 3,
